# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify rewrite rules.
#
# Share links from the app are /join/<slug>. There is one page behind them; the
# slug is read off the path by school.html. A 200 rewrite rather than a 302, so
# the path the user was sent survives into the address bar for the page to parse.
#
# The file is school.html and not join.html on purpose. Workers static assets
# map /join onto join.html automatically, and that mapping fires before this
# rule — /join/nus was being redirected to /join with the slug thrown away.
/join/*   /school   200
